Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Task notes: write notes on a task, shown on its lead or
 deal
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A note written on a task is an ordinary FCRM Note that references the task
(reference_doctype "CRM Task"). No DocType or schema changes. The lead's or
deal's Notes tab and timeline include the notes on its tasks, and the notes
follow the task if it moves to another record.

- crm.api.task: add_note, get_notes, set_status (status and note in one
  request) and suggest_note_title (calls a crm_task_note_title hook)
- activities.get_linked_notes: include notes on the record's tasks
- CRMTask.on_trash: re-point the task's notes to its lead or deal, or delete
  them when it has none (the dynamic link would block the delete)
- FCRMNote.notify_mentions: resolve a task note to the task's parent
- Task dialog: Notes section with an inline composer; note cards say which
  task they were written on

Modified by Másquetú, 2026-11-26.

